      "title": "Middle East crisis: Trump says Iran will make a deal after US midterms – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/sep/22/middle-east-iran-irgc-donald-trump-mahmoud-mahmoud-pezeshkian-abbas-araqchi-unga-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>This live blog is now closed.</p><p></p><p>Tehran appears to have relaxed its preconditions for reopening the strait of Hormuz, saying it is prepared to do so within seven days so long as the US takes reciprocal steps to ease the pressure on Iran.</p><p>Previously Iran had set seven onerous pre-conditions for lifting the blockade including “an end to war on all fronts” and a commitment by the US to cease all aggressive actions against Iran including sanctions.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/sep/22/middle-east-iran-irgc-donald-trump-mahmoud-mahmoud-pezeshkian-abbas-araqchi-unga-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-22T19:09:42"
    },
    {
      "title": "Up to 169 killed in Yemen as Houthis battle for Red Sea coastal heights",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/22/yemen-houthis-battle-strategic-red-sea-heights",
      "description": "<p>Thousands flee fighting as Iran-aligned group seeks to consolidate territorial gains against Saudi-backed government forces</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/sep/22/middle-east-iran-irgc-donald-trump-mahmoud-mahmoud-pezeshkian-abbas-araqchi-unga-latest-news-updates\">Middle East live – latest updates</a></p><p></p></li></ul><p>As many as 169 people have been reportedly killed in Yemen in the last three days as Iran-aligned Houthis battle Saudi-backed government forces for control of strategic heights on the Red Sea coast, while thousands flee the violence.</p><p>Houthi military officials said at least 118 people had been killed in clashes as well as Saudi air and artillery strikes on Taiz, al-Jawf, Marib and Saada provinces since Sunday, Agence France-Presse reported. Yemeni government sources have said at least 36 people have been killed on their side of the conflict.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/22/yemen-houthis-battle-strategic-red-sea-heights\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-22T13:57:36"
    },
